## Require English for all comments

Context: Agents and contributors were not explicitly required to write comments
in English. Canonical Cursor rules (imported by Claude via CLAUDE.md) and the
existing Claude skills now state that code comments, docstrings, and
agent-written notes must be English. No new skill — project convention, not a
technique. UI copy / localisation is out of scope.

Changes:

1. .cursor/01-expertise-and-principles.mdc
   Personal-style bullet: all comments in English; rewrite non-English comments
   when touched.
2. .cursor/05-code-style-and-structure.mdc
   New §Comments — English-only for every comment syntax; why not what.
3. .cursor/08-testing-and-deployment.mdc
   Docstrings must be English.
4. src/.coding_rules.md
   Long-form §3 comments rule + code-review checklist item 11.
5. CLAUDE.md
   Tone reminder pointing at `.cursor/05 §Comments` (no duplicated full rule).
6. .claude/skills/code-review/SKILL.md
   Quick-reference: non-English comments → `.cursor/05 §Comments`.
7. .claude/skills/refactoring/SKILL.md
   Don't add or leave non-English comments.
8. .claude/skills/adding-subpackage/SKILL.md
   Don't write non-English comments/docstrings.
9. .claude/skills/changelog/SKILL.md
   Changelog prose is English only.

