## English-only changelogs, logs, and audit trail

Context: The English-only rule covered comments but was easy to miss for
`/changelogs/`, `logger.*` templates, and domain audit-trail text when the
user writes in another language. Tightened the canonical rule and skills so
those artifacts stay English regardless of conversation language.

Changes:

1. .cursor/01-expertise-and-principles.mdc
   Personal-style bullet now names changelogs, logs, audit trail, and traces.
2. .cursor/05-code-style-and-structure.mdc
   §English-only artifacts lists `/changelogs/`, logger templates, audit
   trail, MLflow traces; log templates called out under Logging Security.
3. .cursorrules
   Changelog workflow requires English even if the user used another language.
4. .cursor/08-testing-and-deployment.mdc
   Changelog bullet points at the English-only rule.
5. src/.coding_rules.md
   Table of artifacts + logger English note + review checklist item 11.
6. CLAUDE.md, .claude/skills/{changelog,code-review,refactoring,adding-subpackage}/SKILL.md
   Skills and Claude tone reminder aligned with §English-only artifacts.

